{"name":"Rock Solid","hex":"#bdc2bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rock solid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically very solid; very difficult to move.","Very strong and dependable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock_solid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rock Solid","blocks":[{"text":"Rock Solid is the thirteenth studio album by the Commodores, released in 1988. At this time in the band's career, hits were no longer forthcoming, and this album failed to enter the Billboard albums chart. The single, \"Solitaire\", reached No. 51 on the R&B chart. It is the last of the band's albums with keyboard player and founding member Milan Williams, who was fired after a dispute about playing in South Africa."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/Rock_Solid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Solid","wikidata":"Q7354682"},{"title":"Solid","blocks":[{"text":"Solid is a state of matter in which atoms are closely packed and are difficult to move past each other. Solids resist compression, expansion, or external forces that would alter its shape, with the degree of resistance being dependent upon the specific material under consideration. Solids also always possess the least kinetic energy per atom/molecule relative to other phases or, equivalently stated, solids are formed when matter in a fluid phase is cooled below a certain temperature. This temperature is called the melting point of the substance and is an intrinsic property; i.e. independent of how much of the matter there is. The vast majority of substances, when in the solid state, can be arranged in one of a few ubiquitous structures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Insulincrystals.jpg/330px-Insulincrystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solid","wikidata":"Q11438"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fcc_lattice_4.jpg/500px-Fcc_lattice_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fcc_lattice_4.jpg/500px-Fcc_lattice_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model of closely packed atoms within a crystalline solid","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFcc_lattice_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Chrysler_Building_detail.jpg/500px-Chrysler_Building_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Chrysler_Building_detail.jpg/500px-Chrysler_Building_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The pinnacle of New York's Chrysler Building, the world's tallest steel-supported brick building, is clad with stainless steel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChrysler_Building_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Different_minerals.jpg/500px-Different_minerals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Different_minerals.jpg/1280px-Different_minerals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Different_minerals.jpg/500px-Different_minerals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A collection of various minerals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADifferent_minerals.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Si3N4bearings.jpg/500px-Si3N4bearings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai